1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,370
Far from any tower, a phone shows just one thing. No signal.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,076
When a building collapses, the person who needs help most can't call for it.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,205
Meet Ranger. A pocket radio messenger that works with no towers, no SIM card, and no internet.

4
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:44,064
Its long range LoRa radio reaches up to eight kilometers in open line of sight. At shorter range, it moves data at up to two hundred and two kilobits per second.

5
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:59,712
And every Ranger is also a relay. Messages hop from device to device, forming a mesh. Add more Rangers, and the network stretches far beyond the reach of any single radio. Every message is encrypted.

6
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,776
See everyone in range, at a glance.

7
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:12,186
Send texts to one person, or to everyone, with delivery confirmation.

8
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:17,075
Hold VOICE to talk, like a walkie-talkie, but private.

9
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:23,561
Track a teammate. The arrow points the way, and shows the distance.

10
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:31,073
No GPS? Ranger measures distance using the radio signal itself.

11
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,300
Check your position, and share it in one press.

12
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:42,891
In an emergency, one press sends an SOS with your location to every Ranger.

13
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,663
It sleeps to save power, and wakes the moment a message arrives.

14
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:59,449
No Ranger? Join one with your phone over Wi-Fi. No app, and no mobile data. Your phone can even lend Ranger its GPS and clock.

15
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:12,928
In a remote desert, a patrol stays in contact across open ground, with nothing to rely on but each other.

16
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:19,644
Under the rubble, a survivor's Ranger carries their voice to the rescue team above.

17
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:28,515
Lost in the jungle, a hiker's message hops across the mesh until it reaches the search team.

18
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,701
And on the trail, friends always know where each other are.

19
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:44,595
Inside: an ESP32 brain, a LoRa radio, an OLED screen, a digital mic, an amplifier, and GPS with a compass.

20
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:52,202
Built to scale, Ranger is expected to cost around three thousand rupees per unit in mass production.

21
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:06,503
Ranger. When the network goes down, you stay connected. Scan the code to see how it's built.

